  "output": {
    "answer": "No gate caught the idle tab — it was a full day's pricing-API allowance plus purchased credits burned over about 7 hours before I traced the drop in daily remaining and called it: the box's Chrome had been left open on a live stream. That's what caught it, after the fact. The watchdog built afterward is a heartbeat that reads the Chrome tab list every 2 hours and reports any live page still open. That's the fastest flagging the record shows now — I don't have a record of a faster or real-time cost-overrun alert beyond that 2-hour heartbeat check.",
